{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Bread [he sifts].</b> And the custom of grain is that it be sifted." "The alef of <b>אדוש</b> is added like the alef of אזרועך (Jeremiah 32:21)." "<b>And he threshes, etc.</b> And at the time he sets the wheel of his cart in motion, then his horses do not thresh it; and the meaning is like when he plows, he does not thresh it, for everything in its time HaShem created to be so; therefore, 'after this also,' etc., the meaning being that he does not thresh it forever."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:43.115994968Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}